      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes that should be OK.  The use case is that user must press the power button to confirm an action (either start diagnostics or to enable developer mode).  In both cases, coreboot should pop the physical presence state prior to showing the user dialog screen prompting for a power button press.  The user shouldn\u0027t be allowed to \"pre-press\" the power button to skip a confirmation dialog.  This is all getting added because the keyboard is untrusted when the EC is closed source.",
